completed gpt-6.1-terra medium None
VERDICT REVISE
The button can send incomplete or stale answers, and its text does not reliably meet the comment size and character requirements.
- {"id": "DD-01", "severity": "high", "path": "docs/decision-desk.html:154", "evidence": "Clicking Done directly from a note field triggers the existing focusout save, but doneText reads S.answers immediately, before that asynchronous write and its snapshot complete. The comment can therefore contain the previous note. The same race applies to a recently selected answer whose snapshot has not arrived.", "fix": "Track pending answer writes and construct the notification from the current drafts and confirmed answer state. Coordinate delivery with those writes while preserving the comments API's gesture requirement, and report a save failure."}
- {"id": "DD-02", "severity": "medium", "path": "docs/decision-desk.html:159", "evidence": "The limit uses JavaScript string length, which counts UTF-16 code units rather than UTF-8 bytes. A 3,000-character note of three-byte characters remains below the 3,500-character threshold but produces a comment well above 4 KiB. Whitespace replacement also leaves control characters such as U+0000 in notes, IDs, or choices.", "fix": "Sanitize control characters in every interpolated field and enforce the limit on the UTF-8 encoded text, truncating safely at character boundaries."}
- {"id": "DD-03", "severity": "medium", "path": "docs/decision-desk.html:157", "evidence": "When the assembled text exceeds the limit, slicing the whole string can remove later decisions or cut a choice or note in the middle. The resulting message still claims the full count is ready to apply, and the success status gives no indication that the notification omitted answers.", "fix": "Preserve complete decision identifiers and choices within the byte budget, explicitly identify omitted or truncated content, and direct the receiving session to read the answers collection for the complete data."}
- {"id": "DD-04", "severity": "medium", "path": "docs/decision-desk.html:161", "evidence": "The Done button is enabled while decisions and answers are still loading. A click before either snapshot arrives can send 'Nothing new is answered' and write an empty ids array even when saved answers exist. Decision loading is tracked, but answer loading is not.", "fix": "Keep the button unavailable until both collections have successfully loaded authoritative snapshots, and provide a retry or chat instruction when either load fails."}
- {"id": "DD-05", "severity": "medium", "path": "docs/decision-desk.html:170", "evidence": "When sending is unavailable, a successful signals/done write is reported as 'Saved for the next session,' but the inspected Decision Desk workflow tells sessions to read the answers collection and contains no reader for signals/done. The signal alone does not establish that a later session will notice the completion event.", "fix": "Add a documented consumer for signals/done, including how it detects and acknowledges new signals, or change the status to avoid promising that a later session will pick it up."}

