ca23655 Decision Desk: done blocks after a failed save, ids in signals/done, says ahead if a session listens (Codex round 3)
exit 0
/private/tmp/claude-2d5c93b0-desk/artifacts/claudex-gy6go3x0/
completed gpt-6.1-terra medium None
VERDICT REVISE
The completion flow has unresolved races that can send before the latest answer is saved, and some failure paths leave the user without the promised fallback.
- {"id": "DD-12", "severity": "high", "path": "docs/decision-desk.html:160", "evidence": "The click handler checks pending writes and failures only before awaiting canSendToClaude() and anchorFor(). While either call is pending, the answer controls remain usable. A user can start an answer write, or that write can fail, before sendToClaude() runs; the notification then tells Claude to read answers while the latest answer is still pending or failed.", "fix": "Prevent answer edits throughout the send operation, or recheck pending writes and failures immediately before sending and abort with a retry message if either changed."}
- {"id": "DD-13", "severity": "medium", "path": "docs/decision-desk.html:180", "evidence": "When a note textarea has focus, clicking the done button first fires focusout. That starts write(), which synchronously disables the button while the pointer gesture is still in progress. The click on the now-disabled button can be suppressed, so the note saves but no completion notification is sent; the user must press again without being told to do so.", "fix": "Handle the completion gesture explicitly: flush the focused note, wait for its write to succeed, and then continue the same requested send, or clearly prompt the user to press again after saving."}
- {"id": "DD-14", "severity": "medium", "path": "docs/decision-desk.html:134", "evidence": "Failures are tracked only by decision ID, and any later successful write or clear for that ID deletes the failure. If two operations for one decision overlap and the newer operation fails before the older operation succeeds, the older success clears the newer failure. Once both settle, done can send even though the latest requested change failed.", "fix": "Serialize operations per decision or track operation versions so only a successful retry of the latest intended state can clear its failure."}
- {"id": "DD-15", "severity": "medium", "path": "docs/decision-desk.html:174", "evidence": "The signals/done write failure is silently ignored. When no session is available, the pre-press hint says pressing saves a note, but a rejected database write saves no signal; a later session has no durable completion record. The user is not told that saving failed.", "fix": "Handle the signal write rejection and report that the completion signal was not saved, with the chat fallback. Avoid promising that pressing saves a note before the write succeeds."}
- {"id": "DD-16", "severity": "medium", "path": "docs/decision-desk.html:193", "evidence": "The initial await claude.use(\"db\") is outside a try/catch, and the fallback timers are installed only after it and the user capability check resolve. If either capability request rejects or never resolves, initialization stops or stalls with the button disabled and the initial status text still displayed instead of the required chat fallback. A decisions snapshot error after successful loading similarly disables the button without updating the done status.", "fix": "Start the loading timeout before awaiting capabilities, catch database initialization errors, and set an explicit chat fallback on decisions snapshot errors."}
